From 265041631ebfdf28799320177ecf20c6bd58356f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:55:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] u_vbuf: NULL-check the translate object (fix aarch64/V3D
 crash on unsupported format)

u_vbuf_translate_buffers() used the translate object from translate_cache_find()
without checking it. translate_generic_create() can return NULL (e.g. a
pure-integer input with an illegal int->output combo, or a CALLOC failure).
Upstream never checks because x86 has translate_sse covering all formats; on
aarch64 (Phoenix-RTOS RPi4 / V3D) only translate_generic exists, so an
unsupported combo yields NULL and the subsequent tr->set_buffer()/tr->run()
dereferenced NULL -> SIGSEGV (owner HW: quake3 crash mid-combat, far=0x3a0,
u_vbuf_translate_begin). Return PIPE_ERROR instead; the caller already treats a
translate failure as "skip this draw's translate" (debug_warn_once + goto out),
so the game continues instead of crashing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit f342ce502820f346a515b151911740961b2a7241)
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c
index 882f683e2a3..f6c64334d4c 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_vbuf.c
@@ -468,6 +468,18 @@ u_vbuf_translate_buffers(struct u_vbuf *mgr, struct translate_key *key,
    /* Get a translate object. */
    tr = translate_cache_find(mgr->translate_cache, key);
 
+   /* translate_cache_find() -> translate_create() -> translate_generic_create()
+    * can return NULL — e.g. for a pure-integer input format with an illegal
+    * int->output combo (is_legal_int_format_combo). Upstream never checks because
+    * on x86 translate_sse covers everything; on aarch64 (Phoenix-RTOS RPi4/V3D)
+    * only translate_generic exists, so an unsupported combo yields NULL and the
+    * unchecked tr->set_buffer()/tr->run() below dereferenced it -> crash (owner HW:
+    * quake3 SIGSEGV mid-combat, u_vbuf_translate_begin, far=0x3a0). Fail the
+    * translate cleanly instead; the caller (u_vbuf_translate_begin) treats a
+    * failure as "skip this draw's translate" rather than crashing. */
+   if (!tr)
+      return PIPE_ERROR;
+
    /* Map buffers we want to translate. */
    mask = vb_mask;
    while (mask) {
